{"id":"03bd3c68487fe2b957058ab2ce4bc5212a91aa89","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"03bd3c68487fe2b957058ab2ce4bc5212a91aa89","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/features/reasoning_outputs.md","lines":["@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ vLLM currently supports the following reasoning models:"," | [MiniMax-M2](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2) | `minimax_m2_append_think` | `json`, `regex` | ✅ |"," | [Qwen3 series](https://huggingface.co/collections/Qwen/qwen3-67dd247413f0e2e4f653967f) | `qwen3` | `json`, `regex` | ✅ |"," | [QwQ-32B](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/QwQ-32B) | `deepseek_r1` | `json`, `regex` | ✅ |","+| [Ripple-65B Preview](https://huggingface.co/ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview) | `ripple` | `json`, `regex` | ✅ |"," | [Step-3.5 / Step-3.7 Flash](https://huggingface.co/stepfun-ai/Step-3.5-Flash) | `step3p5` | `json`, `regex` | ✅ |"," | [ZAYA1 series](https://huggingface.co/Zyphra/ZAYA1-8B) | `zaya` | `json`, `regex` | ✅ |"," ","@@ -40,6 +41,7 @@ vLLM currently supports the following reasoning models:","     Gemma 4 reasoning is disabled by default; to enable it, pass `enable_thinking=True` in your `chat_template_kwargs` or set `reasoning_effort` (which enables it automatically).","     DeepSeek-V3.1 tool calling is supported in non-thinking mode.","     Holo2 reasoning is enabled by default. To disable it, you must also pass `thinking=False` in your `chat_template_kwargs`.","+    Ripple decides per turn whether to reason and has no switch for it. Structured outputs apply from the first token, so constrained responses answer without reasoning.","     Kolibri 1 reasoning is enabled by default. To disable it, set `reasoning_effort=\"none\"` or pass `enable_thinking=False` in your `chat_template_kwargs`."," "," ## Quickstart"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/features/tool_calling.md","lines":["@@ -629,6 +629,18 @@ Flags: `--enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser zaya --reasoning-parser zay"," "," `zaya_xml` is an alias of `zaya`."," ","+### Ripple Models (`ripple`)","+","+Supported models:","+","+* `ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview`","+* `ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4`","+","+Ripple emits Hermes-style JSON tool calls inside `<tool_call>` tags after an","+optional `<think>` block. Pair it with `--reasoning-parser ripple`.","+","+Flags: `--enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser ripple --reasoning-parser ripple`","+"," ### Models with Pythonic Tool Calls (`pythonic`)"," "," A growing number of models output a python list to represent tool calls instead of using JSON. This has the advantage of inherently supporting parallel tool calls and removing ambiguity around the JSON schema required for tool calls. The `pythonic` tool parser can support such models."],"additions":12,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/models/supported_models.md","lines":["@@ -467,6 +467,7 @@ th {"," | `Qwen3ForCausalLM` | Qwen3 | `Qwen/Qwen3-8B`, etc. | ✅︎ | ✅︎ |"," | `Qwen3MoeForCausalLM` | Qwen3MoE | `Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B`, etc. | ✅︎ | ✅︎ |"," | `Qwen3NextForCausalLM` | Qwen3NextMoE | `Qwen/Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B-Instruct`, etc. | ✅︎ | ✅︎ |","+| `RicursiveForCausalLM` | Ripple | `ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview`, `ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4`, etc. | | ✅︎ |"," | `Rnj1ForCausalLM` | Rnj1 | `EssentialAI/rnj-1-instruct`, etc. | | |"," | `SarvamMoEForCausalLM` | Sarvam 2 | `sarvamai/sarvam2-30b-a3b`, etc. | ✅︎ | ✅︎ |"," | `SarvamMLAForCausalLM` | Sarvam 2 | `sarvamai/sarvam2-105b-a9b`, etc. | | ✅︎ |"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"recipes/models/ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview.yaml","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@","+# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://recipes.vllm.ai/recipe.schema.json","+meta:","+  title: \"Ripple-65B-Preview\"","+  slug: \"ripple-65b-preview\"","+  provider: \"Ricursive Intelligence\"","+  description: \"Ricursive's Ripple-65B Preview, a dense 65B model for reasoning and agentic coding with hybrid sliding-window and NoPE full attention, tool calling, and a DFlash2 speculative drafter.\"","+  date_added: 2026-11-04","+  date_updated: 2026-11-04","+  tasks:","+    - text","+  related_recipes: []","+  hardware:","+    b300: verified","+  default_hardware: b300","+","+model:","+  model_id: \"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview\"","+  min_vllm_version: \"0.33.0\"","+  nightly_required: true","+  docker_image: \"vllm/vllm-openai:nightly\"","+  architecture: dense","+  parameter_count: \"65B\"","+  active_parameters: \"65B\"","+  context_length: 2097152","+  base_args: []","+  base_env: {}","+","+features:","+  reasoning:","+    description: \"Ripple reasoning parser: splits an optional leading `<think>` block into `reasoning_content`.\"","+    args:","+      - \"--reasoning-parser\"","+      - \"ripple\"","+  tool_calling:","+    description: \"Ripple tool-call parser with automatic tool choice.\"","+    args:","+      - \"--enable-auto-tool-choice\"","+      - \"--tool-call-parser\"","+      - \"ripple\"","+  spec_decoding:","+    label: \"DFlash2\"","+    description: \"DFlash2 speculative decoding with Ricursive's drafter.\"","+    args:","+      - \"--speculative-config\"","+      - '{\"method\":\"dflash\",\"model\":\"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-DFlash2\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":7}'","+","+opt_in_features:","+  - spec_decoding","+","+variants:","+  default:","+    model_id: \"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4\"","+    precision: nvfp4","+    # Mixed precision, sized from the checkpoint: 57.2 GB × 1.2.","+    vram_minimum_gb: 69","+    description: \"ModelOpt NVFP4 MLPs; attention, embeddings and LM head in BF16.\"","+  bf16:","+    precision: bf16","+    # 129.6 GB × 1.2","+    vram_minimum_gb: 156","+    description: \"Native BF16 checkpoint.\"","+","+compatible_strategies:","+  - single_node_tp","+","+hardware_overrides: {}","+","+strategy_overrides: {}","+","+guide: |","+  ## Overview","+","+  [Ripple-65B Preview](https://huggingface.co/ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview)","+  is a dense 65B model from Ricursive Intelligence. Its 80 layers alternate four","+  1024-token sliding-window layers with one NoPE full-attention layer, and it","+  supports a 2M-token context. The NVFP4 checkpoint fits on one B200/B300.","+","+  Ripple decides per turn whether to reason, so `reasoning_content` is empty","+  when it answers directly.","+","+  ## Client usage","+","+  ```bash","+  curl http://localhost:8000/v1/chat/completions \\","+    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\","+    -d '{","+      \"model\": \"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4\",","+      \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Write a Python function that reverses a linked list.\"}]","+    }'","+  ```","+","+  ## References","+","+  - [Ripple-65B Preview](https://huggingface.co/ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview)","+  - [Ripple-65B Preview NVFP4](https://huggingface.co/ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4)","+  - [DFlash2 drafter](https://huggingface.co/ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-DFlash2)","+  - [vLLM PR #65745](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/65745)"],"additions":97,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/models/registry.py","lines":["@@ -537,6 +537,10 @@ def check_available_online(","         \"Qwen/Qwen3-Next-80B-A3B-Instruct\",","         extras={\"tiny-random\": \"tiny-random/qwen3-next-moe\"},","     ),","+    \"RicursiveForCausalLM\": _HfExamplesInfo(","+        \"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview\",","+        extras={\"nvfp4\": \"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4\"},","+    ),","     \"Rnj1ForCausalLM\": _HfExamplesInfo(","         \"EssentialAI/rnj-1-instruct\",","         is_available_online=False,","@@ -1549,6 +1553,12 @@ def check_available_online(","         is_available_online=False,","         use_original_num_layers=True,","     ),","+    \"DFlash2RicursiveDraftModel\": _HfExamplesInfo(","+        \"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-NVFP4\",","+        speculative_model=\"ricursiveAI/Ripple-65B-Preview-DFlash2\",","+        is_available_online=False,","+        use_original_num_layers=True,","+    ),","     \"DFlashLagunaForCausalLM\": _HfExamplesInfo(","         \"poolside/Laguna-XS-2.1-NVFP4\",","         speculative_model=\"poolside/Laguna-XS-2.1-DFlash-NVFP4\","],"additions":10,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/parser/engine/test_replay.py","lines":["@@ -80,11 +80,11 @@ def _discover_parsers() -> list[_ParserInfo]:","         if cfg.name not in _BUILDERS:","             missing_builders.append(f\"{obj.__name__} (config.name={cfg.name!r})\")","             continue","-        if cfg.name in (\"inkling\", \"plamo3\", \"minimax_m3\"):","-            # Inkling uses typed structural blocks. PLaMo and MiniMax M3","-            # markers can span several token IDs. None fits this TOOL_END-token","-            # harness; their direct and delegating coverage lives in dedicated","-            # tests.","+        if cfg.name in (\"inkling\", \"plamo3\", \"minimax_m3\", \"ripple\"):","+            # Inkling uses typed structural blocks. PLaMo, MiniMax M3 and","+            # Ripple markers can span several token IDs. None fits this","+            # TOOL_END-token harness; their direct and delegating coverage lives","+            # in dedicated tests.","             continue","         if cfg.name == \"granite\":","             # Granite has a JSON-array tool body with no TOOL_END terminal, so"],"additions":5,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/parser/engine/test_ripple.py","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@","+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+\"\"\"Ripple parser: optional ``<think>`` reasoning and JSON tool calls.","+","+The generation prompt does not open ``<think>``, so output without it is the","+answer. The chat template frames markers with newlines, which must not leak","+into reasoning or content.","+\"\"\"","+","+import json","+","+import pytest","+","+from tests.parser.engine.conftest import make_mock_tokenizer","+from tests.parser.engine.replay_harness import (","+    _test_request,","+    collect_output,","+    replay_streaming,","+)","+from vllm.parser.engine.registered_adapters import (","+    RippleParserReasoningAdapter,","+    RippleParserToolAdapter,","+)","+from vllm.parser.parser_manager import ParserManager","+from vllm.parser.ripple import RippleParser","+from vllm.reasoning import ReasoningParserManager","+from vllm.tool_parsers import ToolParserManager","+","+TOOLS = [","+    {","+        \"type\": \"function\",","+        \"function\": {","+            \"name\": \"get_weather\",","+            \"parameters\": {","+                \"type\": \"object\",","+                \"properties\": {\"city\": {\"type\": \"string\"}},","+            },","+        },","+    },","+]","+","+","+def _call(city: str) -> str:","+    body = {\"name\": \"get_weather\", \"arguments\": {\"city\": city}}","+    return f\"\\n<tool_call>\\n{json.dumps(body)}\\n</tool_call>\"","+","+","+# (model output, reasoning, content, tool-call cities)","+CASES = {","+    \"direct_answer\": (\"17*23 = 391.\", \"\", \"17*23 = 391.\", []),","+    \"reasoning\": (","+        \"<think>\\nCompute.\\n17*23=391.\\n</think>\\nThe answer is 391.\",","+        \"Compute.\\n17*23=391.\",","+        \"The answer is 391.\",","+        [],","+    ),","+    \"reasoning_then_tool\": (","+        \"<think>\\nNeed the tool.\\n</think>\" + _call(\"Paris\"),","+        \"Need the tool.\",","+        \"\",","+        [\"Paris\"],","+    ),","+    \"content_then_tools\": (","+        \"Checking both.\" + _call(\"Paris\") + _call(\"Rome\"),","+        \"\",","+        \"Checking both.\",","+        [\"Paris\", \"Rome\"],","+    ),","+    \"truncated_reasoning\": (\"<think>\\nStill thinking\", \"Still thinking\", \"\", []),","+    # Text before a tool call keeps its whitespace in both parse paths.","+    \"extra_newline_before_tool_content\": (","+        \"<think>\\nNeed the tool.\\n</think>\\n\\nChecking now.\" + _call(\"Paris\"),","+        \"Need the tool.\",","+        \"\\nChecking now.\",","+        [\"Paris\"],","+    ),","+}","+","+","+@pytest.fixture","+def tokenizer():","+    return make_mock_tokenizer({\"<|im_start|>\": 1, \"<|im_end|>\": 2})","+","+","+@pytest.fixture","+def parser_cls():","+    return ParserManager.get_parser(","+        tool_parser_name=\"ripple\",","+        reasoning_parser_name=\"ripple\",","+        enable_auto_tools=True,","+    )","+","+","+def test_parser_names_resolve_to_engine_adapters():","+    tool_parser_cls = ToolParserManager.get_tool_parser(\"ripple\")","+    assert issubclass(tool_parser_cls, RippleParserToolAdapter)","+    assert tool_parser_cls.structural_tag_model == \"hermes\"","+    assert (","+        ReasoningParserManager.get_reasoning_parser(\"ripple\")","+        is RippleParserReasoningAdapter","+    )","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"case\", CASES)","+def test_parse(parser_cls, tokenizer, case):","+    text, reasoning, content, cities = CASES[case]","+    parsed_reasoning, parsed_content, tool_calls = parser_cls(tokenizer).parse(","+        text, _test_request(TOOLS), enable_auto_tools=True","+    )","+    assert (parsed_reasoning or \"\") == reasoning","+    assert (parsed_content or \"\") == content","+    assert [json.loads(tc.arguments)[\"city\"] for tc in tool_calls or []] == cities","+    assert all(tc.name == \"get_weather\" for tc in tool_calls or [])","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"chunk_size\", [1, 3])","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"case\", CASES)","+def test_streaming_matches_parse(parser_cls, tokenizer, case, chunk_size):","+    text, reasoning, content, cities = CASES[case]","+    tokens = [(ord(ch), ch) for ch in text]","+    output = collect_output(","+        replay_streaming(","+            parser_cls(tokenizer),","+            tokens,","+            chunk_size=chunk_size,","+            finished_on_last=True,","+            tools=TOOLS,","+        )","+    )","+    assert output.reasoning == reasoning","+    assert output.content == content","+    assert [json.loads(tc[\"arguments\"])[\"city\"] for tc in output.tool_calls] == cities","+","+","+@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"case\", [\"direct_answer\", \"reasoning\"])","+def test_streaming_without_tool_parser(tokenizer, case):","+    # Without --enable-auto-tool-choice no tool parser is composed, so the","+    # reasoning parser alone must still split out <think> while streaming.","+    parser_cls = ParserManager.get_parser(reasoning_parser_name=\"ripple\")","+    assert parser_cls is not None","+    text, reasoning, content, _ = CASES[case]","+    output = collect_output(","+        replay_streaming(","+            parser_cls(tokenizer),","+            [(ord(ch), ch) for ch in text],","+            chunk_size=1,","+            finished_on_last=True,","+            prompt_token_ids=[1, ord(\"u\"), 2, 1],","+        )","+    )","+    assert (output.reasoning, output.content) == (reasoning, content)","+","+","+def test_structured_output_applies_from_first_token(tokenizer):","+    # Thinking is optional, so a constrained response must not wait for a","+    # \"</think>\" the model may never emit.","+    parser = RippleParser(tokenizer)","+    assert parser.is_reasoning_end([1, ord(\"u\"), 2, 1])"],"additions":158,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/parser/engine/trace_builder.py","lines":["@@ -46,8 +46,10 @@","     NemotronV3Parser,","     Plamo3Parser,","     Qwen3Parser,","+    RippleParser,","     SeedOssParser,","     Step3p5Parser,","+    ZayaParser,"," )"," "," # ── Data structures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────","@@ -464,6 +466,20 @@ def _build_step3p5(scenario: Scenario, validate: bool = True) -> Sample:","     )"," "," ","+def _build_zaya(scenario: Scenario, validate: bool = True) -> Sample:","+    \"\"\"ZAYA1: the Qwen3 grammar with ``<zyphra_tool_call>`` tags.\"\"\"","+    sample = _build_qwen3(scenario, name=\"zaya\", validate=False)","+    rename = {\"<tool_call>\": ZayaParser.TOOL_START, \"</tool_call>\": ZayaParser.TOOL_END}","+    sample = replace(","+        sample,","+        vocab={rename.get(text, text): tid for text, tid in sample.vocab.items()},","+        tokens=[(tid, rename.get(text, text)) for tid, text in sample.tokens],","+    )","+    if validate:","+        _validate_sample(sample, ZayaParser)","+    return sample","+","+"," # ── MiniMax M2 (XML invoke format, starts in REASONING) ──────────────"," "," _MINIMAX_M2_VOCAB: dict[str, int] = {","@@ -1244,6 +1260,42 @@ def _build_plamo3(scenario: Scenario, validate: bool = True) -> Sample:","     return sample"," "," ","+# ── Ripple (optional plain-text <think>, JSON tool calls) ────────────","+","+","+def _ripple_segments(scenario: Scenario) -> list[tuple[str, bool]] | None:","+    if scenario.tool_calls is not None and not scenario.tool_calls:","+        return None","+    text = \"\"","+    if scenario.reasoning is not None:","+        text += f\"<think>\\n{scenario.reasoning}\\n</think>\\n\"","+    text += scenario.content or \"\"","+    for tc in scenario.tool_calls or []:","+        body = json.dumps({\"name\": tc.name, \"arguments\": tc.arguments})","+        text += f\"\\n<tool_call>\\n{body}\\n</tool_call>\"","+    return [(text, False)]","+","+","+def _build_ripple(scenario: Scenario, validate: bool = True) -> Sample | None:","+    segments = _ripple_segments(scenario)","+    if segments is None:","+        # Ripple's template never emits an empty tool block.","+        return None","+    sample = _make_sample(","+        sample_id=f\"ripple-{scenario.id}\",","+        description=scenario.description,","+        vocab={},","+        segments=segments,","+        expected_reasoning=scenario.reasoning or \"\",","+        expected_content=_qwen3_expected_content(scenario),","+        expected_tool_calls=_expected_tc(scenario),","+        tools=_expected_tools(scenario),","+    )","+    if validate:","+        _validate_sample(sample, RippleParser)","+    return sample","+","+"," # ── Granite (JSON-array tool bodies, no reasoning) ───────────────────────"," "," _GRANITE_VOCAB: dict[str, int] = {","@@ -1347,6 +1399,8 @@ def _build_granite(scenario: Scenario, validate: bool = True) -> Sample:","     \"step3p5\": _build_step3p5,","     \"inkling\": _build_inkling,","     \"plamo3\": _build_plamo3,","+    \"ripple\": _build_ripple,","+    \"zaya\": _build_zaya,"," }"," "," "],"additions":54,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dflash2.py","lines":["@@ -817,6 +817,52 @@ def forward(self, hidden_states):","     assert [projection.calls for projection in projections] == [1, 1]"," "," ","+def test_ripple_draft_skips_context_rope_on_nope_layers(monkeypatch):","+    \"\"\"The Ripple drafter routes to its own class, whose context keys carry RoPE","+    exactly where the layer's queries do.\"\"\"","+    from torch import nn","+","+    from vllm.config.speculative import SpeculativeConfig","+    from vllm.model_executor.models import qwen3_dflash","+    from vllm.model_executor.models.ricursive_dflash2 import RicursiveDFlash2Model","+","+    def draft_config(**kwargs):","+        config = SimpleNamespace(","+            architectures=[\"DFlash2DraftModel\"], model_type=\"qwen3\", **kwargs","+        )","+        config.update = lambda d: config.__dict__.update(d)","+        return config","+","+    routed = SpeculativeConfig.hf_config_override(draft_config(no_rope_layers=[1]))","+    assert routed.architectures == [\"DFlash2RicursiveDraftModel\"]","+    plain = SpeculativeConfig.hf_config_override(draft_config())","+    assert plain.architectures == [\"DFlash2DraftModel\"]","+","+    def fake_rope(positions, query, key, head_size, cache, is_neox):","+        # Marks rotated keys with 100 + position.","+        query.add_(positions[:, None].to(query.dtype) + 100)","+","+    monkeypatch.setattr(qwen3_dflash.ops, \"rotary_embedding\", fake_rope)","+    model = RicursiveDFlash2Model.__new__(RicursiveDFlash2Model)","+    nn.Module.__init__(model)","+    model.config = SimpleNamespace(no_rope_layers=[1])","+    model._rope_cos_sin_cache = torch.zeros(1)","+    model._rope_head_size = 4","+    model._rope_is_neox = True","+","+    num_layers, num_ctx, head_dim = 3, 2, 4","+    keys = torch.arange(num_layers * num_ctx * head_dim, dtype=torch.float32)","+    keys = keys.view(num_layers, num_ctx, 1, head_dim)","+    all_k = keys.clone()","+    positions = torch.tensor([5, 6])","+    model._apply_context_rope(all_k, positions)","+","+    rotated = keys + (positions.float() + 100).view(1, num_ctx, 1, 1)","+    torch.testing.assert_close(all_k[0], rotated[0])","+    torch.testing.assert_close(all_k[1], keys[1])","+    torch.testing.assert_close(all_k[2], rotated[2])","+","+"," def test_score_edges_keeps_out_of_vocabulary_anchors_in_range():","     \"\"\"A request in chunked prefill anchors on its next prompt token, which can","     lie past the draft vocabulary (a multimodal placeholder).\"\"\""],"additions":46,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"tools/pre_commit/test_tethering_allowlist.txt","lines":["@@ -135,6 +135,7 @@ tests/parser/engine/test_plamo3.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake inst"," tests/parser/engine/test_qwen3.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation"," tests/parser/engine/test_qwen3_reasoning.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation"," tests/parser/engine/test_replay.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation","+tests/parser/engine/test_ripple.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation"," tests/parser/engine/test_seed_oss.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation"," tests/parser/engine/test_step3p5.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation"," tests/parser/engine/test_token_id_scanner.py  # CI jobs disabled pending locked cmake installation"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"vllm/config/speculative.py","lines":["@@ -779,6 +779,12 @@ def hf_config_override(","  